/*
  ClimateSection.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 feature view · 0291 · ClimateSection (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Every key the native
  `ClimateSection` resolves (table "ClimateSection") lives here with its web
  `t(key, default)` English value. These entries fold into the app
  `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept in a
  per-surface table so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings without
  editing the shared catalog.

  The first group is the exact set of keys extracted from the web source
  (features/vehicles/components/vehicle-detail/ClimateSection.tsx — the title, the eight
  MetricCard labels, the "Level" / "On" / "Off" value words, and the empty message),
  reusing the web `vehicles.detail.*` / `common.*` namespaces verbatim. The second group
  backs the native chrome (the P4 leaf freshness / loading / error copy) so the Swift
  sources hold no English prose literals. The temperature unit symbols ("°C" / "°F") and
  the raw fan integer / defrost mode are device/data literals carried in code, not
  translated strings.
*/

